  "description": "Document 113 event contract for the events app/modules/packaging/commands.py actually emits. 6 of the catalogue's 11 declared Document 16 events are implemented: PackagingRunStarted, LineClearanceCompleted, LabelIssued, LabelReconciliationCompleted, PackagingReconciliationCompleted, PackagingCompleted. LabelPrinted, LabelReprinted, LabelApplied, LabelMismatchDetected and PackageAggregated are declared in 07_EVENT_CATALOGUE.yaml but have no producing code path -- this module models label issuance and reconciliation as a single controlled step (LabelIssued -> LabelReconciliationCompleted) rather than tracking print/reprint/apply/mismatch as separate signed events, and does not yet implement multi-unit package aggregation. Verified directly against source, not assumed. KNOWN DEFECT (SG-174, not fixed here): app/modules/equipment/cleaning_commands.py also emits the literal event_type \"LineClearanceCompleted\" (Document 39 equipment/cleanroom line clearance) -- a genuine cross-module name collision in running code. See event-eqp-002.json.",
